SUMMARY:Conn Peak at Lake Hennessey
DESCRIPTION:Go Wild Hikers\nIt's time for another trip to Lake Hennessey. 
 We'll hike up to Conn Peak overlooking the lake. At the top there's a picn
 ic table and a cool stone labyrinth. Moore Creek Park is 1\,600 acres of r
 ugged terrain including Oak woodlands\, Douglas Fir & Madrone forest\, gra
 sslands\, and chaparral. Wildlife in the park is plentiful\, including lar
 ge mammals such as black bears\, mountain lions\, bobcat\, gray fox and co
 yote. Best for individuals with at least a moderate level of fitness.\n\n*
 *Important information**\nIf you've enjoyed hiking with this group\, follo
 w me as I move Go Wild Hikers to a new platform by the end of May called H
 eylo.com\n\nIt's people like you that have made this group so great!! Than
 k you all for being members of Go Wild Hikers and I appreciate the large n
 umber of Hikers who have already followed the group to Heylo. The Shiloh H
 ike on Sunday May 31 still has some room.\n**Upcoming events for Go Wild H
 ikers in June will include Hood Mtn\, Taylor Mtn\, Annadel and North Sonom
 a Mtn to Jack London.**\n[https://heylo.com/invite/PpURbZWX](http://clicks
 .meetup.com/ls/click?upn=u001.NY3oBFzZ5LJDG7YcnfSAKgvWkdmOX3k5-2FX9Cwzxfa6
 ZYDGAbpDzbtJiez6KtS8H-2Fj8h8_7Hv-2FAQY7Bu3bAT0Za4bdMLW62VLMEvpqfEu65buaFe3
